 the design, manufacture, and sale of firearms worldwide. It offers handguns, including revolvers and pistols; long guns, such as modern sporting rifles, pistol caliber carbines, and lever-action rifles; handcuffs; suppressors; and other firearm-related products. It also provides manufacturing services comprising forging, heat treating, rapid prototyping, tooling, finishing, plating, machining, and custom plastic injection molding, assembly, and distribution services to other businesses; and sells parts purchased through third parties. The company sells its products to firearm enthusiasts, collectors, hunters, sportsmen, competitive shooters, individuals desiring home and personal protection, law enforcement, security agencies and officers, and military agencies. It markets its products through independent dealers, retailers, in-store retails, and direct to consumers, and range operations; print, broadcast, and digital advertising campaigns; social and electronic media; and in-store retail merchandising strategies. In addition, the company manufactures firearm accessories and other products, such as headwear, apparel, accessories, magazines, and closeouts. Smith & Wesson Brands, Inc. was formerly known as American Outdoor Brands Corporation and changed its name to Smith & Wesson Brands, Inc. in June 2020. The company was founded in 1852 and is based in Maryville, Tennessee.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Mark Peter Smith | President, CEO & Director | Age 49 | Compensation: $2.1M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $380K ranks in the above the sector median among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $66K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $6K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Smith & Wesson Brands, Inc. is a small-cap industrials business with a $649M market cap on $524M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years and -3% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 11% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, with gross margins sitting at 35%.","The business throws off $90M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 17 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 6.18\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","Accruals are elevated at -18.7% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 5.4\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 3.6% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 19% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Payout ratio of 96% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"News sentiment sharply negative (-0.38) across 12 recent articles \u2014 the narrative has turned","sev":"red","cat":"news"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 50/100): structural revenue/margin decline; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 53% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Trading the Move, Not the Narrative: (SWBI) Edition","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/149/Trading_the_Move,_Not_the_Narrative:_SWBI_Edition_110326071602_1793751362.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793751362.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What Smith & Wesson Brands Buyers Were Betting On","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/consumer-durables/nasdaq-swbi/smith-wesson-brands/news/what-smith-wesson-brands-buyers-were-betting-on","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793787663.766,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.202,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Missed Smith & Wesson Brands' Run? Here's The Bet Holders Made","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/missed-smith-wesson-brands-run-181032855.html","date":"2026-10-31","timestamp":1793470232.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.433,"tier":1,"